<?xml version="1.0"?>
<psalm
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xmlns="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config"
        xsi:schemaLocation="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config vendor-bin/psalm/vendor/vimeo/psalm/config.xsd"
        xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"
        resolveFromConfigFile="true"
>
    <projectFiles>
        <directory name="src" />

        <ignoreFiles>
            <directory name="vendor" />
        </ignoreFiles>
    </projectFiles>

    <!--
        Psalm 6 turns on several checks that were not running under the 4.x line this project
        previously pinned. Most were addressed rather than silenced:

        findUnusedCode is left enabled. It reported 25 PossiblyUnusedMethod and 3 ClassMustBeFinal
        because whole-project unused-code analysis cannot see a library's consumers. Marking the
        three published classes @api resolves both, and is a better answer than switching the
        check off, because genuinely dead private and internal code is still reported.

        The three RiskyTruthyFalsyComparison findings were fixed by making the null and
        empty-string cases explicit.

        What remains cannot be fixed here:

        MissingOverrideAttribute wants #[\Override], which is PHP 8.3 and up. This package
        supports 8.2, so the attribute cannot be applied unconditionally. Worth revisiting if the
        floor ever moves to 8.3 — which would also allow PHPUnit 12.

        RedundantCast is all ten instances of (string) $e->getAwsErrorMessage(). Psalm infers that
        as non-null, but the SDK documents it @return string|null, and the cast is what stops a
        null reaching ClientException's string parameter as a TypeError. Psalm's stub is more
        optimistic than the source it describes.
    -->
    <issueHandlers>
        <MissingOverrideAttribute errorLevel="suppress" />
        <RedundantCast errorLevel="suppress" />
    </issueHandlers>
</psalm>
